  "name": "web: one malformed db file 500s every page and leaks filesystem paths/stack traces",
  "slug": "web-one-malformed-db-file-500s-every-page-and-leaks-filesyst",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "readJsoncDir throws on the first corrupt/schema-drifted file, and listTickets/findTicketByRef call it for every view — so one bad file breaks /tickets, /tree, /review, /stale, and even an unrelated ticket detail. Bun.serve runs in dev mode (no NODE_ENV) so the 500 body leaks the server filesystem path and a stack trace.",
    "details_md": "",
    "acceptance": [
      "Per-file parse/validate errors are caught and the bad file is skipped+logged (or surfaced as an N failed to load banner) rather than failing the whole listing",
      "slop web runs Bun.serve with development:false (or gated on an explicit flag) so local runs do not leak stack traces/paths",
      "A test points one ticket file at invalid content and asserts other views still render 200"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/web/fixture-data-source.ts:50-69 readJsoncDir/parseEntity (uncaught throw)",
      "src/cli/commands/web.ts (no NODE_ENV / development flag)"
    ],
